IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 1 (continued): ss 2A to 2D (online communication services) and the Fourth Schedule.
-- These rules state the 2024 consolidation. Section 2A and the Fourth Schedule entered with Act 38 of 2022
-- (wef 1 February 2023, as the annotations in the text say); the text before that was not obtained, so a seat
-- question that depends on them gates by date (sgba-seat.l4).
-- Forward reference: "social media service" has the meaning given by s 45T (module sgba-p10a-meanings.l4); here it is
-- a plain fact, `the service is a social media service as section 45T defines it`.

§ `2A. Meanings of "online communication service" and associated terms`

-- src:639 | 2A.—(1) In this Act, an online communication service means an
-- src:640 | electronic service that is, or a part of an electronic service having the
-- src:641 | characteristics that are, specified in the Fourth Schedule.
@ref s 2A(1) (src:639-641)
GIVEN `the electronic service has the characteristics specified in the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(1) the service, or the part of it, is an online communication service` MEANS
    `the electronic service has the characteristics specified in the Fourth Schedule`

-- src:643 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), an electronic service means a
-- src:644 | service —
-- src:646 | (a) that —
-- src:648 | (i) enables end-users to access or communicate content
-- src:649 | on the Internet using that service, including a point-
-- src:650 | to-multipoint service; or
-- src:652 | (ii) delivers content on the Internet to persons having
-- src:653 | equipment appropriate for receiving that content,
-- src:654 | where the delivery of the service is by a service
-- src:655 | described in sub‑paragraph (i);
@ref s 2A(2)(a) (src:643-655)
GIVEN `it enables end-users to access or communicate content on the Internet using the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it delivers content on the Internet to persons with appropriate equipment, the delivery being by a service of that first kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(2)(a) the service is of the kind the paragraph describes` MEANS
    `it enables end-users to access or communicate content on the Internet using the service`
    OR `it delivers content on the Internet to persons with appropriate equipment, the delivery being by a service of that first kind`

-- src:657 | (b) that is a service —
-- src:659 | (i) between a point in Singapore and one or more other
-- src:660 | points in Singapore; or
-- src:665 | (ii) between a point and one or more other points, where
-- src:666 | the firstmentioned point is outside Singapore and at
-- src:667 | least one of the other points is inside Singapore; and
@ref s 2A(2)(b) (src:657-667)
GIVEN `it is between a point in Singapore and one or more other points in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its first point is outside Singapore and at least one other point is inside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(2)(b) the service is between points as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    `it is between a point in Singapore and one or more other points in Singapore`
    OR `its first point is outside Singapore and at least one other point is inside Singapore`

-- src:669 | (c) that is not an excluded electronic service.
@ref s 2A(2)(c) (src:669)
GIVEN `the service is an excluded electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(2)(c) the service is not an excluded electronic service` MEANS
    NOT `the service is an excluded electronic service`

-- src:643 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), an electronic service means a
-- src:644 | service —
-- src:646 | (a) that —
-- src:648 | (i) enables end-users to access or communicate content
-- src:649 | on the Internet using that service, including a point-
-- src:650 | to-multipoint service; or
-- src:652 | (ii) delivers content on the Internet to persons having
-- src:653 | equipment appropriate for receiving that content,
-- src:654 | where the delivery of the service is by a service
-- src:655 | described in sub‑paragraph (i);
-- src:657 | (b) that is a service —
-- src:659 | (i) between a point in Singapore and one or more other
-- src:660 | points in Singapore; or
-- src:665 | (ii) between a point and one or more other points, where
-- src:666 | the firstmentioned point is outside Singapore and at
-- src:667 | least one of the other points is inside Singapore; and
-- src:669 | (c) that is not an excluded electronic service.
@ref s 2A(2) (src:643-669)
GIVEN `paragraph (a) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(2) the service is an electronic service` MEANS
    `paragraph (a) is met` AND `paragraph (b) is met` AND `paragraph (c) is met`

-- src:671 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(c), an excluded electronic
-- src:672 | service means —
-- src:674 | (a) an SMS service;
-- src:676 | (b) an MMS service;
-- src:678 | (c) an internet access service;
-- src:680 | (d) an electronic service where the only user-generated content
-- src:681 | enabled by that service is one-to-one live aural
-- src:682 | communications;
-- src:684 | (e) an electronic service where the only user-generated content
-- src:685 | enabled by that service is communication between 2 or
-- src:686 | more end-users that is of a private or domestic nature;
-- src:688 | (f) an electronic service where the user-generated content
-- src:689 | enabled by that service is accessible substantially or only to
-- src:690 | a closed group of end-users employed or engaged in a
-- src:691 | business (whether or not carried on for profit) and solely
-- src:692 | for their use as a tool in the conduct of that business; or
-- src:694 | (g) an electronic service that is prescribed by the Minister, by
-- src:695 | order in the Gazette, to be an excluded electronic service,
-- src:696 | after taking into account the functionalities of the service
-- src:697 | or the user-generated content enabled by that service or
-- src:698 | both.
@ref s 2A(3) (src:671-698)
GIVEN `it is an SMS service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an MMS service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an internet access service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its only user-generated content is one-to-one live aural communications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its only user-generated content is communication between 2 or more end-users of a private or domestic nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its user-generated content is accessible substantially or only to a closed group of end-users employed or engaged in a business, solely for their use as a tool in the conduct of that business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has prescribed it by order in the Gazette to be an excluded electronic service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(3) the service is an excluded electronic service` MEANS
        `it is an SMS service`
    OR `it is an MMS service`
    OR `it is an internet access service`
    OR `its only user-generated content is one-to-one live aural communications`
    OR `its only user-generated content is communication between 2 or more end-users of a private or domestic nature`
    OR `its user-generated content is accessible substantially or only to a closed group of end-users employed or engaged in a business, solely for their use as a tool in the conduct of that business`
    OR `the Minister has prescribed it by order in the Gazette to be an excluded electronic service`

-- src:700 | (4) References in this Act to an online communication service
-- src:701 | include such a service provided from outside Singapore as well as
-- src:702 | such a service provided in or from Singapore.
@ref s 2A(4) (src:700-702)
-- A reference to an online communication service takes in one provided from outside Singapore as well as one
-- provided in or from Singapore: so where the service is provided from is no bar.
GIVEN `the service is provided from outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(4) the place the service is provided from stops it being an online communication service` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:704 | (5) In this section —
-- src:706 | “functionality”, in relation to an electronic service, includes —
-- src:708 | (a) any feature that enables interactions of any
-- src:709 | description between end-users of the service; and
-- src:714 | (b) any feature that enables end-users to search online
-- src:715 | locations or databases, index search results or
-- src:716 | otherwise retrieve content from the search results;
@ref s 2A(5) "functionality" (src:704-716)
GIVEN `it is a feature that enables interactions of any description between end-users of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a feature that enables end-users to search online locations or databases, index search results or otherwise retrieve content from the search results` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2A(5) the feature is a functionality of the electronic service` MEANS
    IF `it is a feature that enables interactions of any description between end-users of the service`
       OR `it is a feature that enables end-users to search online locations or databases, index search results or otherwise retrieve content from the search results`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:718 | “MMS” means an electronic service that enables only the
-- src:719 | transmission of multimedia messages (such as visual or voice
-- src:720 | communication) from an end-user on a mobile telephone to
-- src:721 | another mobile telephone through a telecommunication
-- src:722 | service;
-- src:724 | “MMS message” means a message (whether or not accompanied
-- src:725 | by any sound or images) sent using an MMS;
@ref s 2A(5) "MMS" and "MMS message" (src:718-725)
GIVEN `it enables only the transmission of multimedia messages from an end-user on a mobile telephone to another mobile telephone through a telecommunication service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(5) the electronic service is an MMS` MEANS
    `it enables only the transmission of multimedia messages from an end-user on a mobile telephone to another mobile telephone through a telecommunication service`

-- src:724 | “MMS message” means a message (whether or not accompanied
-- src:725 | by any sound or images) sent using an MMS;
@ref s 2A(5) "MMS message" (src:724-725)
GIVEN `it was sent using an MMS` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(5) the message is an MMS message` MEANS
    `it was sent using an MMS`

-- src:727 | “one-to-one live aural communications”, in relation to an
-- src:728 | electronic service, means content —
-- src:730 | (a) consisting of speech or other sounds conveyed in real
-- src:731 | time between 2 end-users of the service by means of
-- src:732 | the service;
-- src:734 | (b) that is not a recording; and
-- src:736 | (c) that is not accompanied by user-generated content of
-- src:737 | any other description, except identifying content;
@ref s 2A(5) "one-to-one live aural communications" (src:727-737)
GIVEN `it consists of speech or other sounds conveyed in real time between 2 end-users of the service by means of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a recording` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accompanied by user-generated content of another description other than identifying content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(5) the content is one-to-one live aural communications` MEANS
    `it consists of speech or other sounds conveyed in real time between 2 end-users of the service by means of the service`
    AND (NOT `it is a recording`)
    AND (NOT `it is accompanied by user-generated content of another description other than identifying content`)

-- src:739 | “point-to-multipoint service” means an electronic service which
-- src:740 | allows an end-user to communicate content to more than one
-- src:741 | end-user simultaneously;
@ref s 2A(5) "point-to-multipoint service" (src:739-741)
GIVEN `it allows an end-user to communicate content to more than one end-user simultaneously` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(5) the electronic service is a point-to-multipoint service` MEANS
    `it allows an end-user to communicate content to more than one end-user simultaneously`

-- src:743 | “SMS” means an electronic service that only enables the
-- src:744 | transmission of short text messages from an end-user on a
-- src:745 | mobile telephone to another mobile telephone through a
-- src:746 | telecommunication service;
-- src:748 | “SMS message” means a text message sent using an SMS;
@ref s 2A(5) "SMS" and "SMS message" (src:743-748)
GIVEN `it only enables the transmission of short text messages from an end-user on a mobile telephone to another mobile telephone through a telecommunication service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(5) the electronic service is an SMS` MEANS
    `it only enables the transmission of short text messages from an end-user on a mobile telephone to another mobile telephone through a telecommunication service`

-- src:748 | “SMS message” means a text message sent using an SMS;
@ref s 2A(5) "SMS message" (src:748)
GIVEN `it is a text message sent using an SMS` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(5) the message is an SMS message` MEANS
    `it is a text message sent using an SMS`

-- src:750 | “user-generated content”, in relation to an electronic service,
-- src:751 | means content —
-- src:753 | (a) that is —
-- src:755 | (i) generated directly on the service by an end-user
-- src:756 | of the service; or
-- src:758 | (ii) communicated by posting or sharing on the
-- src:759 | service by an end-user of the service; and
-- src:764 | (b) that may be accessed by another end-user of that
-- src:765 | service, or other users, of the service by means of that
-- src:766 | service.
@ref s 2A(5) "user-generated content" (src:750-766)
GIVEN `it is generated directly on the service by an end-user of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is communicated by posting or sharing on the service by an end-user of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it may be accessed by another end-user, or other users, of the service by means of the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2A(5) the content is user-generated content` MEANS
    `it may be accessed by another end-user, or other users, of the service by means of the service` AND (`it is generated directly on the service by an end-user of the service` OR `it is communicated by posting or sharing on the service by an end-user of the service`)

§ `2B. Amendment of Fourth Schedule`

-- src:772 | 2B.—(1) The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, revoke or
-- src:773 | replace, or add to, the Fourth Schedule.
@ref s 2B(1) (src:772-773)
-- The Minister's power: what it means for a person is that the Fourth Schedule can change by order in the Gazette.
GIVEN `the Minister has made an order in the Gazette revoking, replacing or adding to the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2B(1) the Fourth Schedule has been changed by order` MEANS
    `the Minister has made an order in the Gazette revoking, replacing or adding to the Fourth Schedule`

-- src:775 | (2) Every order made under subsection (1) must be presented to
-- src:776 | Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the Gazette.
@ref s 2B(2) (src:775-776)
GIVEN `the order has been presented to Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2B(2) the order has been presented to Parliament as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the order has been presented to Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the Gazette`

§ `2C. Transitional arrangements for former licensable broadcasting service`

-- src:783 | 2C.—(1) With effect from the date that a licensable broadcasting
-- src:784 | service is specified in the Fourth Schedule as an online
-- src:785 | communication service (called the conversion date) —
-- src:787 | (a) this Act ceases to apply to —
-- src:789 | (i) that service as a licensable broadcasting service; and
-- src:791 | (ii) the provider of that service as a broadcasting
-- src:792 | licensee; and
-- src:794 | (b) this Act then continues to apply to that service as an online
-- src:795 | communication service, and the former broadcasting
-- src:796 | licensee as a provider of an online communication service,
@ref s 2C(1)(a) and (b) (src:783-796)
-- On the conversion date the Act stops applying to the service as a licensable broadcasting service and to its
-- provider as a broadcasting licensee, and goes on applying to it as an online communication service.
GIVEN `the date is on or after the conversion date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2C(1)(a) this Act still applies to the service as a licensable broadcasting service` MEANS
    IF `the date is on or after the conversion date` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the date is on or after the conversion date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2C(1)(a)(ii) this Act still applies to the provider as a broadcasting licensee` MEANS
    IF `the date is on or after the conversion date` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the date is on or after the conversion date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2C(1)(b)(ii) this Act continues to apply to the former licensee as a provider of an online communication service` MEANS
    IF `the date is on or after the conversion date` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:783 | 2C.—(1) With effect from the date that a licensable broadcasting
-- src:784 | service is specified in the Fourth Schedule as an online
-- src:785 | communication service (called the conversion date) —
-- src:794 | (b) this Act then continues to apply to that service as an online
-- src:795 | communication service, and the former broadcasting
-- src:796 | licensee as a provider of an online communication service,
@ref s 2C(1)(b) (src:783-796)
GIVEN `the date is on or after the conversion date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2C(1)(b) this Act continues to apply to the service as an online communication service` MEANS
    IF `the date is on or after the conversion date` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:798 | but without affecting the following:
-- src:800 | (c) the enforcement by any person of any right or claim against
-- src:801 | the former broadcasting licensee;
-- src:803 | (d) the enforcement by the former broadcasting licensee of any
-- src:804 | right or claim against any person;
-- src:806 | (e) any proceeding under section 12(1) with respect to the
-- src:807 | former licensable broadcasting service that is pending
-- src:808 | immediately before the conversion date;
-- src:813 | (f) any appeal under section 12(2) or 59(1) with respect to the
-- src:814 | former licensable broadcasting service that is pending
-- src:815 | immediately before the conversion date.
@ref s 2C(1)(c) to (f) (src:798-815)
-- Four things the conversion does not affect.
GIVEN `it is the enforcement of a right or claim, or a pending proceeding under section 12(1), or a pending appeal under section 12(2) or 59(1), concerning the former licensable broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2C(1)(c)-(f) the conversion affects it` MEANS
    IF `it is the enforcement of a right or claim, or a pending proceeding under section 12(1), or a pending appeal under section 12(2) or 59(1), concerning the former licensable broadcasting service`
    THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:817 | (2) Any proceeding and appeal mentioned in subsection (1)(e) and
-- src:818 | (f) may be continued under sections 12 and 59, respectively, as if the
-- src:819 | Fourth Schedule had not been enacted.
@ref s 2C(2) (src:817-819)
GIVEN `it is a proceeding or appeal mentioned in section 2C(1)(e) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2C(2) the proceeding or appeal may be continued under sections 12 and 59 as if the Fourth Schedule had not been enacted` MEANS
    IF `it is a proceeding or appeal mentioned in section 2C(1)(e) or (f)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `2D. Meaning of "provider" of online communication service`

-- src:825 | 2D.—(1) Subject to this section, in this Act, the provider of an
-- src:826 | online communication service is the entity that has control over —
-- src:828 | (a) who can use the online communication service that is
-- src:829 | specified in the Fourth Schedule;
-- src:831 | (b) the operations of the characteristics of the electronic
-- src:832 | service that are specified in the Fourth Schedule in respect
-- src:833 | of the online communication service; or
-- src:835 | (c) which content is communicated or provided on the online
-- src:836 | communication service.
@ref s 2D(1) (src:825-836)
GIVEN `it controls who can use the online communication service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it controls the operations of the characteristics of the electronic service specified in the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it controls which content is communicated or provided on the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2D(1) the entity is the provider of the online communication service` MEANS
    `it controls who can use the online communication service`
    OR `it controls the operations of the characteristics of the electronic service specified in the Fourth Schedule`
    OR `it controls which content is communicated or provided on the service`

-- src:838 | (2) Where an online communication service is generated by a
-- src:839 | machine, the entity that controls the machine (and that entity alone) is
-- src:840 | to be treated as being the provider of the online communication
-- src:841 | service.
@ref s 2D(2) (src:838-841)
GIVEN `the service is generated by a machine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity controls the machine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2D(2) the entity, and that entity alone, is treated as the provider` MEANS
    IF `the service is generated by a machine` THEN JUST `the entity controls the machine` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:843 | (3) However, if no entity controls the machine mentioned in
-- src:844 | subsection (2), but an individual controls or individuals control the
-- src:845 | machine, the provider of the online communication service is to be
-- src:846 | treated as being that individual or those individuals.
@ref s 2D(3) (src:843-846)
GIVEN `the service is generated by a machine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no entity controls the machine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an individual or individuals control the machine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2D(3) the individual or individuals who control the machine are treated as the provider` MEANS
    IF `the service is generated by a machine` AND `no entity controls the machine`
    THEN JUST `an individual or individuals control the machine` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:848 | (4) If no entity has control over —
-- src:850 | (a) who can use the online communication service that is
-- src:851 | specified in the Fourth Schedule;
-- src:853 | (b) the operations of the characteristics of the electronic
-- src:854 | service that are specified in the Fourth Schedule in respect
-- src:855 | of the online communication service; or
-- src:857 | (c) which content is communicated or provided on the online
-- src:858 | communication service,
-- src:863 | but an individual has or individuals have control over who can do so,
-- src:864 | then that individual or those individuals is or are to be treated as being
-- src:865 | the provider of the online communication service.
@ref s 2D(4) (src:848-865)
GIVEN `no entity has control over who can use the service, the operations of the characteristics, or which content is communicated or provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an individual has or individuals have control over who can do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2D(4) the individual or individuals are treated as the provider` MEANS
    IF `no entity has control over who can use the service, the operations of the characteristics, or which content is communicated or provided`
    THEN JUST `an individual has or individuals have control over who can do so` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:867 | (5) Despite subsection (1), a person that provides an internet access
-- src:868 | service through which content on an online communication service
-- src:869 | may be accessed by end-users of the online communication service, is
-- src:870 | not to be treated as a person who has control over who can use the
-- src:871 | online communication service for the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 2D(5) (src:867-871)
GIVEN `the person provides an internet access service through which content on the online communication service may be accessed by its end-users` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2D(5) the person is treated as having control over who can use the online communication service` MEANS
    IF `the person provides an internet access service through which content on the online communication service may be accessed by its end-users`
    THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:873 | (6) Part 10A regulations may be made to specify who is to be
-- src:874 | treated as a provider of an online communication service where more
-- src:875 | than one entity is treated as the provider thereof under subsection (1).
@ref s 2D(6) (src:873-875)
-- Part 10A regulations may name the provider where more than one entity is a provider under s 2D(1): a borrowed fact.
GIVEN `more than one entity is a provider under section 2D(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 10A regulations name one of them as the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2D(6) the regulations' choice decides who is treated as the provider` MEANS
    IF `more than one entity is a provider under section 2D(1)` THEN JUST `Part 10A regulations name one of them as the provider` ELSE NOTHING

§ `Fourth Schedule -- online communication services`

-- src:4411 | 1. Social media service.
-- src:4412 | 2. App distribution service.
@ref Fourth Schedule, Part 1, items 1 and 2 (src:4411-4412)
-- The characteristics are the two items; the meaning of "social media service" is s 45T (module sgba-p10a-meanings.l4).
GIVEN `the service is a social media service as section 45T defines it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is an app distribution service as the Fourth Schedule defines it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Fourth Schedule Part 1 the electronic service has a specified characteristic` MEANS
    `the service is a social media service as section 45T defines it`
    OR `the service is an app distribution service as the Fourth Schedule defines it`

-- src:4418 | 1. In this Schedule —
-- src:4420 | “app” means an application software package that includes content
-- src:4421 | accessible by end-users, or allows end-users to access content on the
-- src:4422 | Internet through the installed application software;
@ref Fourth Schedule, Part 2, item 1, "app" (src:4418-4422)
GIVEN `it is an application software package that includes content accessible by end-users` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an application software package that allows end-users to access content on the Internet through the installed application software` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Fourth Schedule Part 2 the thing is an app` MEANS
    `it is an application software package that includes content accessible by end-users`
    OR `it is an application software package that allows end-users to access content on the Internet through the installed application software`

-- src:4424 | “app distribution service” means an electronic service (that is accessible by
-- src:4425 | Singapore end-users) that is provided for the purpose of enabling end-
-- src:4426 | users to download an app where the download of the app is by means of
-- src:4427 | access to the Internet.
@ref Fourth Schedule, Part 2, item 1, "app distribution service" (src:4424-4427)
GIVEN `it is an electronic service accessible by Singapore end-users` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is provided for the purpose of enabling end-users to download an app` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the download is by means of access to the Internet` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Fourth Schedule Part 2 the service is an app distribution service` MEANS
    `it is an electronic service accessible by Singapore end-users`
    AND `it is provided for the purpose of enabling end-users to download an app`
    AND `the download is by means of access to the Internet`
